messages.content:
## Diagnosis

The two symptoms come from the same code path, which lives *behind* the handler in `AppsSection.vue`:

1. `@select` → `$storex.projects.activeProjectChanged(project)` does the in-place switch, and **as its last step** calls `syncRouteProjectPrefix()`, which runs:
   ```js
   router.replace({ name: targetName, params: { ...current.params, projectName }, query })
   ```
2. That call is *inside* the `try` block of `activeProjectChanged`. In this build the router only exposes the catch-all desktop route (`codx-junior-split`, `path: '/*'`) — there is no project-scoped named route to resolve, so the replace either resolves to `/<project_name>` (native location change → shell torn down, looks like a page reload) or throws synchronously (not caught by `.catch()`) → the action aborts, and the project "doesn't change".

So: the switch must be **store-driven only**, and the URL sync must be skipped when the current route cannot express the project (and must never throw).

## Changes summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/layout/AppsSection.vue` | Replace the inline `@select` call with an explicit, awaited `onProjectSelected()` handler (de-dupe current project, surface errors as notifications, never let a failure escape). No route/URL work in the component. |
| `src/store/project.js` | `syncRouteProjectPrefix()`: no-op on the desktop catch-all route (where the project is not part of the URL), and wrap the `router.replace` in try/catch so a router error can never abort the project switch. |

## Files

